{
  "example": "`fn[load]` moves to `src/config/load.rs` and its body is also edited. The\nmapped node's hash differs from the recorded one, so `habeas refactor` leaves\nevery record that read it unchanged and reports each one; those records stay\nstale until `habeas author` reassesses them.\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.outline_inputs`\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.whole_record`",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The example `requirements.refactor.edited_while_moving` gives a concrete case. `fn[load]` moves to `src/config/load.rs` with its body edited. The expected result is that `habeas refactor` leaves every record that read it unchanged and reports each one, and that the records stay stale.\n\nThe test `tests/refactor.rs#fn[a_function_edited_while_moving_leaves_its_records_stale]` covers this case:\n- **Setup:** `project()` and `author(root)` write current evidence. `move_load(root, \" parse();\")` moves `load` to `src/config/load.rs` and adds `parse();` to its body, so the mapped node's hash differs from the recorded one.\n- **Command:** it runs `refactor` with `--map src/config.rs#fn[load]=src/config/load.rs#fn[load]` and asserts that the command succeeds.\n- **Reported:** it asserts the report contains `- evidence/rules.load.json: inputs[1]: src/config/load.rs#fn[load] no longer has the recorded hash`. That names the record, the input and the failed hash check, which matches `requirements.refactor.outline_inputs` and the \"reports each one\" outcome.\n- **Unchanged:** it compares the bytes of `evidence/rules.load.json` before and after and asserts they are equal. That is the whole-record rule in `requirements.refactor.whole_record`, and it checks that the record is left unchanged.\n- **Stale:** it asserts that `errors(root)` (validation) is non-empty, which shows the records remain stale until reassessed.\n\nIn the fixture built by `author`, `evidence/rules.load.json` is the only record that reads `fn[load]`. The other record reads `fn[check]`, `fn[verify]` and `data.txt`. So \"each one\" is exercised with the single affected record, and the example requires nothing further.\n\nI found no gap.",
